    "updated_at": "2022-12-12T17:48:20Z",
    "body": "I have a [CL](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/4097472) up with the changes to the tests (will update here after it lands). Since the effects of priority are all implementation-specific and not exposed, other than not erroring when they are set there's not much we can test.\r\n\r\nAs far as the IDL import, I pinged @foolip to see if there's a workflow to stop importing it, but I can also remove the fetch integration section from the spec which has the IDL bits (and remove the HTML part when HTML is ready to land). That should also avoid any conflicts. Main question is if I remove them before the fetch changes land or wait until they have landed and there is content to point to from the Priority Hints spec.",
